<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>

    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;netstandard2.1;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageId>OzaLog</PackageId>
    <AssemblyName>OzaLog</AssemblyName>
    <PackageVersion>3.1.1</PackageVersion>
    <RootNamespace>OzaLog</RootNamespace>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>


    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <Features>strict</Features>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>true</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>

    <Description>Lean .NET local file logging library with the simplest possible static API — one line LOG.Info_Log("...") and you're done, no DI, no LoggerFactory. HFT-grade async pipeline: ConcurrentQueue&lt;struct LogItem&gt; + persistent FileStream pool + 1ms cached timestamp + drop-oldest backpressure. Zero NuGet dependencies on net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0. Designed for high-throughput multi-threaded scenarios like cryptocurrency tick streams. NOT related to NLog (jkowalski's package); the previous version "Ozakboy.NLOG" has been deprecated and renamed to OzaLog in v3.0. See https://github.com/ozakboy/OzaLog/blob/main/docs/en/migration.md for upgrade guide.</Description>
    <PackageTags>ozalog;logging;logger;log;dotnet;csharp;nuget;async-logging;file-logging;local-logging;high-performance;hft;zero-dependency;thread-safe;multi-threaded;exception-handling;log-rotation;dotnet-core;dotnet-standard;performance-logging</PackageTags>

    <Title>OzaLog — Lean .NET local file logger</Title>
    <!-- PackageReleaseNotes 由 uplog 指令在每次發版時更新;與英文 changelog 對齊 -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v3.1.1 — Two bug fixes that affect whether you can trust your logs. No API changes, no default value changes.

FIXED:
- Error / Fatal entries (and any call with immediateFlush: true) were written TWICE. AsyncLogHandler.Enqueue queued the item for the dispatcher and also wrote it synchronously on the caller thread, so each entry appeared as two identical lines. If you have been counting errors from your logs, every number before 3.1.1 was double the real count — recalibrate any error-rate alert thresholds. These entries are now written only once, on the caller thread, with the immediate-flush guarantee unchanged; as a side benefit they no longer pass through the queue and can never be discarded by drop-oldest backpressure. Trace / Debug / Info / Warn / CustomName were not affected.
- Synchronous mode (EnableAsyncLogging = false) produced 0-byte log files. The synchronous path wrote into a StreamWriter with AutoFlush = false and nothing ever flushed it — the dispatcher, the periodic disk-flush timer and the ProcessExit hook are all started by the async pipeline, which synchronous mode never reaches, so the content was lost when the process exited. If you have been using synchronous mode, your log files have been empty all along. Synchronous mode now flushes after every entry (no forced fsync), stays thread-safe, and produces formatting identical to asynchronous mode.

TECHNICAL:
- FileStreamPool.Flush gained a flushToDisk parameter (default true; existing behavior unchanged).
- New internal LogText.WriteSync used by the synchronous path.
- New regression tests (DuplicateWriteTests, SyncModeWriteTests); AutoFlushLevelTests still guards LogLevel.CustomName = 99 against being treated as auto-flush.
- Verified across all 5 TargetFrameworks (netstandard2.0/2.1, net8.0/9.0/10.0) with 0 errors.

Full changelog: https://github.com/ozakboy/OzaLog/blob/main/docs/en/changelog.md
Async pipeline details: https://github.com/ozakboy/OzaLog/blob/main/docs/en/async-pipeline.md
Website: https://ozakboy.github.io/OzaLog/

    </PackageReleaseNotes>



    <!-- 版權宣告 -->
    <Authors>ozakboy</Authors>

    <!-- 專案連結 -->
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/ozakboy/OzaLog</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/ozakboy/OzaLog</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>github</RepositoryType>

    <!-- 文件產生設定 -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <DocumentationFile>file.xml</DocumentationFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

    <!-- 套件圖示 (顯示於 NuGet.org 與 IDE 套件管理員) -->
    <PackageIcon>logo.png</PackageIcon>

    <!-- 授權設定 -->
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(TargetFramework)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|netstandard2.1|AnyCPU'">
    <WarningLevel>6</WarningLevel>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(TargetFramework)|$(Platform)'=='Release|netstandard2.1|AnyCPU'">
    <WarningLevel>6</WarningLevel>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\..\README_zh-TW.md"></None>
    <None Include="..\..\logo.png" Pack="True" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    System.Text.Json (STJ) 依賴策略：
    • net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0：STJ 已內建於 BCL，零 NuGet 依賴
    • netstandard2.0 / netstandard2.1：BCL 不含 STJ，需透過 NuGet 引入
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition=" '$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' OR '$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.1' ">
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="9.0.16" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="10.0.300">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
